  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "VLT AQUA Drive FC 202 using the built-in RS-485 (FC) port with 8-30 Protocol = Modbus RTU and the FC control profile; parameter data checked against the software 5.4X programming guide.",
  "summary": "Danfoss's water and wastewater variable frequency drive, with a built-in RS-485 port that can speak Modbus RTU. The control word, bus reference, status word and main actual value sit at fixed holding registers 50000-50210, and every drive parameter is a holding register at ten times its parameter number. This map covers that control block, the communication and comm-loss parameters, the main 15-xx/16-xx readouts, the process feedback and PID setpoint 1.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "parameter-derived",
    "note": "Registers are printed 1-based (the design guide's own rule: register 40001 is address 0, coil 1 is address 0). A parameter's register number is 10 x its parameter number (3-03 -> 3030, 16-13 -> 16130) and the request carries that number minus 1 (16-13 is read at address 16129). The fixed process registers CTW 50000, REF 50010, STW 50200 and MAV 50210 follow the same minus-1 rule (CTW = address 49999). Coil 65 is address 64."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "Programming data per software 5.4X guide; Modbus mapping per Design Guide MG20N602 (09/2014)",
  "source": {
    "title": "Design Guide VLT AQUA Drive FC 202 0.25-90 kW (section 3.8 System Integration: Modbus RTU)",
    "doc_number": "MG20N602",
    "revision_date": "2014-09",
    "url": "https://assets.danfoss.com/documents/272866/AJ300847815559en-000006.pdf",
    "pages": "Design Guide printed pp. 83-90 (PDF 85-92): Modbus network setup (Table 3.33), coil/register addressing and coil tables (p. 85), holding register table 3.39 (p. 86), parameter access x10 rule, IND, coil 65 (p. 87), FC profile CTW (pp. 88-89), STW and REF/MAV scaling (pp. 89-90). Programming Guide software 5.4X (AU361182657213en-002101, 2024.06): 3-02/3-03 p. 123, 3-13 p. 126, 3-41/3-42 p. 131, 4-14/4-18 p. 138, 8-01..8-04 pp. 217-219, 8-10 pp. 221-222, 8-30..8-35 pp. 230-232, 15-00..15-05 pp. 385-386, 16-xx pp. 409-425, 20-21 p. 453."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Programming data source: VLT AQUA Drive FC 202 Programming Guide, software 5.4X, AU361182657213en-002101 (2024.06), https://assets.danfoss.com/documents/397954/AU361182657213en-002101.pdf. Each parameter's conversion index gives the scale: -1 = x0.1, -2 = x0.01, -3 = x0.001, 0 = x1, 1 = x10.",
    "Indices 67, 74, 75 and 100 have no factor printed in the current guide; the older FC 202 Programming Guide MG20OB02 (software 3.30, AU361182657213en-002001, Table 4.1, printed p. 248, https://assets.danfoss.com/documents/274161/AU361182657213en-002001.pdf) gives them 1/60, 3600, 3600000 and 1 relative to SI units, so the transferred integer is already in RPM, hours, kWh and degC (scale 1).",
    "Word order: the design guide says 32-bit parameters use 2 registers but prints no 32-bit example. Danfoss's Modbus RTU Operating Instructions MG92B102 (https://assets.danfoss.com/documents/latest/271338/AQ361181101347en-000101.pdf), written for the Danfoss FC series as a whole and using the same register scheme as this drive's design guide, maps an Int32/Uint32 as bytes 3-2 in the first register and bytes 1-0 in the second (printed p. 17) and its read example for 3-03 at registers 3030/3031 returns 0016E360h = 1500000 (printed p. 22): high word first (ABCD).",
    "16-10 Power [kW] has conversion index 1 and the 5.4X guide states its fieldbus value is in 10 W steps with W as the base unit, so raw x 0.01 = kW.",
    "REF and MAV are signed 16-bit values where 16384 (4000h) = 100%; with 3-00 = min-max the range runs from 3-02 (0%) to 3-03 (100%), with -max..+max it runs from -3-03 to +3-03. Coils 17-32 carry the same reference (0x0-0xFFFF = -200%..~200%).",
    "8-bit parameters (Uint8, e.g. 8-31, 16-18, 16-34) are read and written as one 16-bit register.",
    "16-62/16-64 analog inputs are in volts or milliamps depending on the terminal mode switch/setting; the guide prints no unit for the readout.",
    "Left out: 16-05 Main Actual Value [%] and 16-15 Frequency [%] (normalised N2 type); 16-26 Power Filtered [kW] (index 0, base unit not stated; its description text in the guide is also wrong); 16-50 External Reference (no unit printed); 15-30..15-33 alarm log arrays (need IND); text parameters; option-card and cascade-controller groups.",
    "Alarm/warning/extended status words (16-90..16-95) are listed as raw UINT32; their bit meanings are in the programming guide's troubleshooting tables.",
    "Coils 1-16 / 17-32 / 33-48 / 49-64 mirror CTW, REF, STW and MAV (output frequency in open loop, feedback in closed loop); only coil 65 (parameter write control) is listed separately.",
    "The design guide's 3-14 example prints registers 3410/3411 and '11300 = 1113.00'; by the x10 rule 3-14 is 3140/3141, so treat that example as a typo.",
    "The current FC 202 programming guide no longer documents 3-00 Reference Range; the REF scaling note above comes from the design guide."
  ],
