  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set 8-30 to Modbus RTU and power-cycle, make sure 8-02 points at the FC port and the drive is not in local/Hand control, then write the control word to 50000 and the reference to 50010 and poll 50200/50210. Read readouts from the 16-xx registers at parameter number x 10 (minus 1 on the wire).",
    "minimum_registers": [
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 49999,
        "why": "CTW: start/stop/reset"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 50009,
        "why": "REF: speed reference, 4000h = 100%"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 50199,
        "why": "STW: ready/running/trip/warning"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 16129,
        "why": "16-13 Frequency, 0.1 Hz"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 16139,
        "why": "16-14 Motor current, 0.01 A"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 16099,
        "why": "16-10 Power, 10 W steps (0.01 kW)"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 16519,
        "why": "16-52 Process feedback"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 16899,
        "why": "16-90 Alarm word"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 15019,
        "why": "15-02 kWh counter"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Set 8-30 Protocol = [2] Modbus RTU (effective only after the drive is powered off and on), 8-31 Address (1-247), 8-32 FC Port Baud Rate and 8-33 Parity/Stop Bits. 8-02 Control Word Source must be [1] FC port; 8-01 Control Site picks digital inputs and/or control word; 8-50, 8-53, 8-55 and 8-56 default to Logic OR, which decides how bus bits combine with terminals. STW bit 9 must read 1 (not local) and CTW bit 10 (data valid) must be 1 for the control word to act.",
    "watchdog": "8-03 Control Word Timeout Time (1-18000 s, 0.1 s units) and 8-04 Control Word Timeout Function (default Off; options include Freeze output, Stop, Jogging, Max. speed, Stop and trip, set-up switching, Forced stop and trip, Warning only). A valid control word restarts the timer. 8-05 End-of-Timeout Function (default Resume set-up) and 8-06 Reset Control Word Timeout handle recovery after a set-up-switching timeout.",
    "quirks": [
      "Parameter register = parameter number x 10, request address = that minus 1 (16-13 -> 16130 -> address 16129).",
      "32-bit values are high word first (ABCD).",
      "REF/MAV use 4000h = 100% of the 3-02..3-03 reference range, negative values in two's complement.",
      "CTW bit 10 must be 1 or the whole control word is ignored. Derived from the bit table (no ready-made words are printed): bits 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 10 set = 047Ch runs on the ramp; clearing bit 6 (043Ch) ramps to stop; bit 7 resets on its rising edge.",
      "Uint8 parameters still occupy a full 16-bit register."
    ],
    "setup": [
      "RS-485 on the control-card terminals of the built-in FC port; set the Modbus address 1-247 in 8-31.",
      "The design guide gives even parity, 1 stop bit as the Modbus default (8-33); baud is chosen in 8-32 (2400-115200).",
      "8-35 Minimum Response Delay (5-10000 ms) can be raised for slow masters or RS-485 converters.",
      "Array parameters need the index written to holding register 9 before the read or write."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Parameter writes go to RAM only unless coil 65 is set to 1; RAM-only changes are lost at power-down.",
      "If a fieldbus option is fitted in slot A the drive sets 8-02 to Option A at first power-up, and Modbus control words on the FC port are then ignored.",
      "Pressing [Stop/Reset] on the keypad or setting 3-13 Reference Site to Local blocks bus control (STW bit 9 = 0); a Local setting survives power-down.",
      "8-30 also offers [23] Modbus multi master; it belongs to the drive-to-drive cascade master/follower pump setup (group 27-**, uses set-ups 1 and 2), so a BMS or PLC master should use [2] Modbus RTU."
    ]
  },
